    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d75">

                <pb facs="0349" n="35" sameAs="frus:frus1914Supp/pg35"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 763.72/75</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Antwerp</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Diederich</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <dateline>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Consulate General</hi>, <lb/>
                    <placeName>
                        <hi rendition="#italic">Antwerp</hi></placeName>, <date
                        ana="#date_undated-inferred-from-document-content" calendar="gregorian"
                        notAfter="1914-08-03T13:20:00-05:00" notBefore="1914-08-03T00:00:00+02:00"
                            ><hi rendition="#italic">undated</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Received August 3, 1914, 1:20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                <p rendition="#center">[Telegram]</p>
                <p>Germany asked permission enter Belgian territory which was refused, whereupon
                    martial law declared. Antwerp City in state siege. Situation very grave. Demands
                    immediate relief, protection, provisions, transportation. Thousands of Americans
                    in Antwerp and Belgium.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Consul General</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
